# LLaVA FLAX Conversion Guide

This project involves converting the LLaVA (Large Language and Vision Assistant) model from PyTorch to FLAX for integration with Hugging Face Transformers.

## Key Conversion Steps

1. Analyze PyTorch implementation
2. Identify reusable FLAX components from existing models (especially from LLAMA)
3. Create FLAX equivalents for each PyTorch class, ensuring structure matches safetensor keys
4. Update auto-mapping files for proper integration
5. Add tests and documentation

## Important Files to Create/Modify

### Model Implementation
- `src/transformers/models/llava/modeling_flax_llava.py` (main implementation)
- `src/transformers/models/llava/__init__.py` (expose FLAX classes)

### Integration Files
- `src/transformers/models/auto/modeling_flax_auto.py` (auto-mapping)
- `src/transformers/__init__.py` (public exports)
- `src/transformers/models/__init__.py` (add to model list)

### Testing
- `tests/models/llava/test_modeling_flax_llava.py`
### Documentation
- `docs/source/en/model_doc/llava.md`

## Special Considerations
- Follow the "Copied from" convention for reused code
- Leverage existing LLaVA safetensors for weights (no separate conversion needed)
- Properly handle multimodal aspects (vision+text)
